%% The human-in-the-loop path, which is the product's central claim.
%% Read the alternatives: nothing moves to the tracker without a person.
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant MA as Marcus (author and owner)
  participant BE as Beacon
  participant SA as Sarah (facilitator)
  participant LOG as Decision log
  participant TR as Jira / Azure DevOps

  Note over BE: a day-8 update reads as blocked, but no blocker has been raised
  BE->>BE: raise a hidden-blocker signal. Evidence is the phrases, confidence is inferred with its basis
  BE->>MA: "Your update reads as blocked. Are you blocked?"
  Note over BE,MA: the AUTHOR is asked first. Nobody else is alerted yet, and the question is re-asked every run
  alt Marcus answers yes
    MA->>BE: yes, waiting on the client for credentials
    BE->>SA: proposal preview "Status in progress to blocked" plus a drafted comment, both editable
    SA->>BE: approve, edit, or reject
    BE->>LOG: proposal.decided approved, by Sarah, at this time
    LOG->>TR: the approved change, labelled AI-assisted
    Note over LOG,TR: reversible. event.undone removes its effect without deleting the record
  else Marcus answers no
    MA->>BE: no, it only reads that way
    BE->>LOG: signal.decided dismissed, with a reason
    Note over BE,LOG: the dismissal rate feeds confidence calibration. Above 30 percent the detector is retuned
  else nobody answers
    BE->>SA: escalated on the next run, with the question still unanswered
  end
